  "term": "cross-sectional analysis",
  "definition": "Cross-sectional analysis is the examination of measurements taken at a single point in time within a group to describe their status and explore how those measurements are related to other factors. In the source, it refers to assessing vitamin D levels at hospital discharge and testing their associations with characteristics such as age, season, health conditions, and location.",
